= Practice Questions

#mcq(1, [Consumer protection means:], (
  [protecting sellers from competition], [protecting consumers against unfair, restrictive and deceptive trade practices], [protecting the government's tax revenue], [protecting advertisers from criticism],
))

#mcq(2, [A person who buys goods *for resale* in his shop wants to file a complaint for defects. Under the Act he is:], (
  [a consumer entitled to file], [not a consumer — goods bought for commercial resale fall outside the definition], [a consumer only for services], [entitled to file only through an NGO],
))

#mcq(3, [A consumer's claim is worth ₹1.2 crore. The commission competent to hear it first is the:], (
  [District Commission], [State Commission], [National Commission], [Supreme Court],
))

#mcq(4, [The correct appeal ladder under the 2019 Act runs:], (
  [District $arrow$ National $arrow$ State], [State $arrow$ District $arrow$ National], [District $arrow$ State $arrow$ National $arrow$ Supreme Court], [National $arrow$ State $arrow$ District],
))

#mcq(5, [A defective pressure cooker risks bursting. The consumer right most directly involved is the right to:], (
  [safety], [choose], [be heard], [consumer education],
))

#mcq(6, [Which of the following is a consumer *responsibility*, not a right?], (
  [right to be informed about purity and price], [asking for a cash memo at the time of purchase], [right to seek redressal], [right to consumer education],
))

#mcq(7, [A complaint about a service whose failure occurred on 10 March must be filed by 10 March of which later year?], (
  [the same year], [one year later], [two years later], [three years later],
))

#mcq(8, [The commission orders a company to publish a corrected advertisement after a false claim. The remedy used is:], (
  [refund of price], [replacement of goods], [corrective advertisement], [punitive damages],
))

#mcq(9, [A registered consumer society files a complaint on behalf of an aggrieved villager. Under the Act, this is:], (
  [not permitted — only the consumer may file], [permitted — registered consumer organisations can file complaints], [permitted only with the Government's approval], [permitted only for claims above ₹2 crore],
))

#mcq(10, [An NGO gets shampoo samples tested in its own lab and publishes the results. Its role here is:], (
  [deciding the case as a commission], [testing products and publishing results — a watchdog activity of consumer organisations], [regulating prices], [issuing quality marks like ISI],
))

= Solutions

#solution(1, [Consumer protection is the shield for the *buyer*: laws, forums, awareness and organisations guarding against unfair, restrictive and deceptive trade practices. It protects consumers — not sellers, tax or advertisers.], answer: "B")

#solution(2, [The Act defines a consumer as one buying for *own use or use by a permitted person* — *not for resale or commercial purpose*. A shopkeeper buying stock for resale falls outside the definition.], answer: "B")

#solution(3, [₹1.2 crore sits between the two money walls — above ₹50 lakh and up to ₹2 crore — so the *State Commission* hears it first. The District ceiling is ₹50 lakh; the National floor is ₹2 crore.], answer: "B")

#solution(4, [Appeals climb one tier at a time: *District $arrow$ State $arrow$ National*, and from the National Commission to the *Supreme Court*. Every other order skips or inverts a tier.], answer: "C")

#solution(5, [Protection from goods *hazardous to life and health* is the *right to safety* — the first of the six rights. Being heard and education are separate rights.], answer: "A")

#solution(6, [Asking for and keeping the *cash memo* is a *responsibility* — the buyer's own habit that makes redressal possible. The other three options are rights the system owes.], answer: "B")

#solution(7, [The complaint window is *two years* from the date the cause of action arose — here, 10 March, two years later. One year and three years are distractors.], answer: "C")

#solution(8, [When a false claim must be undone publicly, the commission can order a *corrective advertisement* — one of the ten remedies, aimed at reversing the deception.], answer: "C")

#solution(9, [A *registered consumer organisation* may file a complaint on behalf of any consumer — one of the five doors into the machinery. No government approval or value limit is needed.], answer: "B")

#solution(10, [Independent testing and publishing of results is a classic *watchdog activity* of consumer organisations. Only the commissions decide cases; ISI marks are issued by the BIS, not NGOs.], answer: "B")

